{"capture_path":"sources/captures/ecfr-2026-07-01/section-141.64.xml","capture_sha256":"4f1e79cb54139f1901e4a7d7efbd31408b349b661eeb65929426e1f5302933e4","heading":"§ 141.64 Maximum contaminant levels for disinfection byproducts.","logical_anchors":[{"label":"141.64(a)","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[1]","status":"derived"},{"label":"141.64(a)(1)","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[2]","status":"derived"},{"label":"141.64(a)(2)","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[3]","status":"derived"},{"label":"141.64(b)(1)","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[4]","status":"derived"},{"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[5]","status":"review-item"},{"label":"141.64(b)(2)","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[6]","status":"derived"},{"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[7]","status":"review-item"},{"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[8]","status":"review-item"}],"review_items":[{"designators":["ii"],"kind":"logical-anchor-ambiguity","reason":"designator level ambiguous in context; no label guessed","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[5]"},{"designators":["ii"],"kind":"logical-anchor-ambiguity","reason":"designator level ambiguous in context; no label guessed","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[7]"},{"designators":["iii"],"kind":"logical-anchor-ambiguity","reason":"designator level ambiguous in context; no label guessed","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[8]"}],"section_number":"141.64","tree":{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[1]/I[1]","tag":"I","text":"Bromate and chlorite."}],"kind":"paragraph","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[1]","tag":"P","text":"(a) Bromate and chlorite. The maximum contaminant levels (MCLs) for bromate and chlorite are as follows:"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[1]","tag":"TH","text":"Disinfection byproduct"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[2]","tag":"TH","text":"MCL (mg/L)"}],"kind":"row","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Bromate"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"0.010"}],"kind":"row","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Chlorite"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"1.0"}],"kind":"row","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]","tag":"TR"}],"kind":"table","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]","tag":"TABLE"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]/DIV[1]","tag":"DIV"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[1]","tag":"DIV"},{"children":[{"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[2]/I[1]","tag":"I","text":"Compliance dates for CWSs and NTNCWSs."}],"kind":"paragraph","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[2]","tag":"P","text":"(1) Compliance dates for CWSs and NTNCWSs. Subpart H systems serving 10,000 or more persons must comply with this paragraph (a) beginning January 1, 2002. Subpart H systems serving fewer than 10,000 persons and systems using only ground water not under the direct influence of surface water must comply with this paragraph (a) beginning January 1, 2004."},{"kind":"paragraph","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[3]","tag":"P","text":"(2) The Administrator, pursuant to section 1412 of the Act, hereby identifies the following as the best technology, treatment techniques, or other means available for achieving compliance with the maximum contaminant levels for bromate and chlorite identified in this paragraph (a):"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[1]","tag":"TH","text":"Disinfection byproduct"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[2]","tag":"TH","text":"Best available technology"}],"kind":"row","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Bromate"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"Control of ozone treatment process to reduce production of bromate"}],"kind":"row","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Chlorite"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"Control of treatment processes to reduce disinfectant demand and control of disinfection treatment processes to reduce disinfectant levels"}],"kind":"row","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]","tag":"TR"}],"kind":"table","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]","tag":"TABLE"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]/DIV[1]","tag":"DIV"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[2]","tag":"DIV"},{"kind":"paragraph","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[4]","tag":"P","text":"(b) TTHM and HAA5. (1) Subpart L—RAA compliance. (i) Compliance dates. Subpart H systems serving 10,000 or more persons must comply with this paragraph (b)(1) beginning January 1, 2002. Subpart H systems serving fewer than 10,000 persons and systems using only ground water not under the direct influence of surface water must comply with this paragraph (b)(1) beginning January 1, 2004. All systems must comply with these MCLs until the date specified for subpart V compliance in § 141.620(c)."},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[1]","tag":"TH","text":"Disinfection byproduct"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[2]","tag":"TH","text":"MCL (mg/L)"}],"kind":"row","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Total trihalomethanes (TTHM)"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"0.080"}],"kind":"row","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Haloacetic acids (five) (HAA5)"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"0.060"}],"kind":"row","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]","tag":"TR"}],"kind":"table","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]","tag":"TABLE"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]/DIV[1]","tag":"DIV"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[3]","tag":"DIV"},{"kind":"paragraph","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[5]","tag":"P","text":"(ii) The Administrator, pursuant to section 1412 of the Act, hereby identifies the following as the best technology, treatment techniques, or other means available for achieving compliance with the maximum contaminant levels for TTHM and HAA5 identified in this paragraph (b)(1):"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[4]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[1]","tag":"TH","text":"Disinfection byproduct"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[4]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[2]","tag":"TH","text":"Best available technology"}],"kind":"row","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[4]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[4]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Total trihalomethanes (TTHM) and Haloacetic acids (five) (HAA5)"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[4]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"Enhanced coagulation or enhanced softening or GAC10, with chlorine as the primary and residual disinfectant"}],"kind":"row","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[4]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]","tag":"TR"}],"kind":"table","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[4]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]","tag":"TABLE"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[4]/DIV[1]","tag":"DIV"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[4]","tag":"DIV"},{"kind":"paragraph","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[6]","tag":"P","text":"(2) Subpart V—LRAA compliance. (i) Compliance dates. The subpart V MCLs for TTHM and HAA5 must be complied with as a locational running annual average at each monitoring location beginning the date specified for subpart V compliance in § 141.620(c)."},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[1]","tag":"TH","text":"Disinfection byproduct"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[2]","tag":"TH","text":"MCL (mg/L)"}],"kind":"row","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Total trihalomethanes (TTHM)"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"0.080"}],"kind":"row","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Haloacetic acids (five) (HAA5)"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"0.060"}],"kind":"row","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]","tag":"TR"}],"kind":"table","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]","tag":"TABLE"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]/DIV[1]","tag":"DIV"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[5]","tag":"DIV"},{"kind":"paragraph","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[7]","tag":"P","text":"(ii) The Administrator, pursuant to section 1412 of the Act, hereby identifies the following as the best technology, treatment techniques, or other means available for achieving compliance with the maximum contaminant levels for TTHM and HAA5 identified in this paragraph (b)(2) for all systems that disinfect their source water:"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[6]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[1]","tag":"TH","text":"Disinfection byproduct"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[6]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[2]","tag":"TH","text":"Best available technology"}],"kind":"row","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[6]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[6]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Total trihalomethanes (TTHM) and Haloacetic acids (five) (HAA5)"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[6]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"Enhanced coagulation or enhanced softening, plus GAC10; or nanofiltration with a molecular weight cutoff ≤1000 Daltons; or GAC20"}],"kind":"row","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[6]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]","tag":"TR"}],"kind":"table","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[6]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]","tag":"TABLE"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[6]/DIV[1]","tag":"DIV"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[6]","tag":"DIV"},{"kind":"paragraph","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/P[8]","tag":"P","text":"(iii) The Administrator, pursuant to section 1412 of the Act, hereby identifies the following as the best technology, treatment techniques, or other means available for achieving compliance with the maximum contaminant levels for TTHM and HAA5 identified in this paragraph (b)(2) for consecutive systems and applies only to the disinfected water that consecutive systems buy or otherwise receive:"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[1]","tag":"TH","text":"Disinfection byproduct"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]/TH[2]","tag":"TH","text":"Best available technology"}],"kind":"row","row":1,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[1]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":"Total trihalomethanes (TTHM) and Haloacetic acids (five) (HAA5)"},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"Systems serving ≥10,000: Improved distribution system and storage tank management to reduce residence time, plus the use of chloramines for disinfectant residual maintenance"}],"kind":"row","row":2,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[2]","tag":"TR"},{"children":[{"col":1,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[1]","tag":"TD","text":""},{"col":2,"kind":"cell","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]/TD[2]","tag":"TD","text":"Systems serving <10,000: Improved distribution system and storage tank management to reduce residence time"}],"kind":"row","row":3,"selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]/TR[3]","tag":"TR"}],"kind":"table","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]/TABLE[1]","tag":"TABLE"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]/DIV[1]","tag":"DIV"}],"kind":"other","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/DIV[7]","tag":"DIV"},{"kind":"citation","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]/CITA[1]","tag":"CITA","text":"[71 FR 478, Jan. 4, 2006]"}],"kind":"section","selector":"DIV8[N=141.64]","tag":"DIV8"}}
